-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/dd98a650-e7b4-4080-ae65-03fd24d63b89
-- title:
--   The retained cover and global-key bundle survives prefix preservation
-- statement:
--   Let $f,h,J$ be natural numbers and $\mu,\nu$ integer-valued memories. Suppose $\mu$ stores the complete cover/key bundle based at $f$: the local-cover header and tables, selected schedule rows and candidate indices, the original output-layer masks, and the exact global-key array with its length header. Write $H$ for that key-header address and
--   $$E=H+1+\left(T\binom{512h}{2h}\right)^J,$$
--   where $T$ is the local schedule length. If $\nu(x)=\mu(x)$ for every $x<E$, then
--   $$\operatorname{Stored}(\mu,f,h,J)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\operatorname{Stored}(\nu,f,h,J).$$
--
--   The bundle can therefore be reused by later phases whose writes preserve the prefix ending at the first address after the global keys.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightCoverKeyData.lean#L60-L77

